    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Related: #40921\n\n### Problem\n\nSince ada2007453 (\"feat(dir): provider framework #40738\"), `-` from an unnamed buffer opens the parent of the current directory, instead of the current directory. `-` from a named buffer still opens the current directory.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\ncd some/dir\nnvim --clean file.txt\n-\n# Notice how `dir/` is the listed directory.\n```\n\n```sh\ncd some/dir\nnvim --clean\n-\n# Notice how `some/` is the listed directory.\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`-` opens the current directory, regardless if the buffer is named or not. This would match other similar plugins I'm aware of, and was also the behavior of this plugin up until recently as mentioned. Since the change was not mentioned in the docs or commit message, I assume it is an unintentional regression, but the wanted behavior can still be discussed.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13 commit b0685d311e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNA\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nAlpine Linux v3.24 x86_64, Linux 7.1.4-0-stable\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.27.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nBuild from repo",
