            "body": "> `-` opens the current directory, regardless if the buffer is named or not.\n\nin my experience this is a nice DWIM behavior, it does something useful instead of something dumb.\n\nalso thing `1-` (count=1) is useful to *always* open the effective CWD (`getcwd()`), regardless of current buffer. and `[count]-` (count>1) should go up to the nth parent relative to curbuf.",
